 The current suite covers profile validation, ranking order, explicit ineligibility, work-plan data isolation, human-only submission policy, and structured API-label normalization. The recorded browser scenario fills sourced values, preserves an unknown UEI, saves a draft, and leaves certification unchecked.
 
+## Repair drifted field ids
+
+Portal ids change more often than the questions. The repair command places the playbook field map onto observed controls — selector, label, type, and count — and prints a proposal. It does not read typed values, call a model, rewrite the playbook, or submit the form.
+
+```bash
+./bin/grant-filler repair-fields \
+  skills/agentic-grant-application/playbooks/demo.local.md \
+  fixtures/field-repair/renamed-ids.json
+```
+
+A selector that still matches one control is kept. A field moves only when one label uniquely names it. EIN, SSN, bank account, and award amount move only onto a label that clearly names that field, never onto project id, case number, or reference number. Two controls with the same label are a tie, and any unresolved field blocks the proposal. The JSON field `publishable` says whether the returned map is safe to keep; the command does not write it.
